3. Item 1: mechanical check of every lucide-react import
Method
- Old package: npm pack lucide-react@0.563.0 --ignore-scripts into /tmp/opencode/lucide-old/tgz/. Its sha512 equals the lockfile entry at 7515ae3b.
- New package: node_modules/lucide-react 1.77.0 (dashboard/package-lock.json:8048 to :8050). No npm install or update ran.
- Import scan: 18 import statements in 18 files under dashboard/ name 30 distinct imported names. I scanned 461 source files and excluded node_modules and .next.
- A 19th file, dashboard/__tests__/image-upload-component.test.tsx, mentions lucide-react in comments only.
- dashboard/lib/document-wrapper/icons.ts holds static lucide-static data. It does not import lucide-react.
- Shape check: I rendered each name with 5 prop sets in both CJS builds under React 19.3.1. This gives 150 pairs.
- The 5 prop sets are:
  1. none
  2. className h-4 w-4
  3. size 48, strokeWidth 1.5, and color red
  4. className mr-2 h-6 w-6 text-primary
  5. aria-label x with size 20
- I compared the markup after I removed the class attribute. I ran the check twice: once in the first part of this audit and once again before I wrote this report.

Result
- 30 names, 0 missing, 0 viewBox changes.
- 28 names have identical markup in all 5 prop sets. 2 names change: BookOpen and BookOpenCheck.
- 150 pairs: 140 identical, 10 different. The 10 belong to BookOpen and BookOpenCheck.
- 5 imported names are aliases in 1.77.0, and none has a deprecation mark.
- Class lists differ for 7 names (table 3.3). Default props do not differ.

